[gd_scene load_steps=12 format=3 uid="uid://wardbfixbreaker01"]

; Wall-mounted lighting breaker — room 16's "the breaker switch". Canonical
; size 0.50W x 0.60H x 0.16D, origin at the centre of the volume, faceplate
; faces -Z, matching every other fixture under fixtures/ and the size
; kit.ts's SWITCH_FOOTPRINT authors ([thin 0.16, height 0.60, along 0.50]).
;
; SILHOUETTE IS THE POINT. The dispenser is a slot-and-tray, the keypad is a
; grid of small bumps; this is a flat plate with ONE big thing sticking out of
; it. A player scanning a wall from across the bay has to be able to tell "the
; thing you throw" from "the thing you type into" before either is legible,
; which is why this gets its own accent colour (amber) and its own shape
; rather than a recoloured keypad.
;
; THE LEVER IS A PIVOT NODE, not a mesh. `Lever` sits at the top of the handle
; and everything visible hangs BELOW it, so a room script animating the throw
; only ever writes Lever.rotation.x and the handle swings about its bolt like
; a real one. rooms/room16/room16.gd does exactly that (see LEVER_LIT/
; LEVER_DARK) — it is also why nothing here is baked into a single mesh.
;
; Visuals only — no collision, no gameplay script. The room generator supplies
; the Area3D + CollisionShape3D this gets instanced under.

[ext_resource type="Material" uid="uid://wardbfxbb01" path="res://fixtures/breaker_body_mat.tres" id="m_body"]
